WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:03.000
-Thank you very much.
Enjoy yourself.

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:05.534
Welcome, welcome, welcome to
"The Tonight Show," everybody.

00:00:05.534 --> 00:00:07.801
You're here. You made it.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:07.801 --> 00:00:09.767
Thank you for tuning in at home.

00:00:09.767 --> 00:00:11.167
I'm very excited about this.

00:00:11.167 --> 00:00:14.000
My guest tonight is the
one-and-only Samuel L. Jackson!

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:15.033
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Whoa!

00:00:15.033 --> 00:00:18.400
♪♪
-Yes!

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:20.934
I bumped into him backstage,
and he was cursing like crazy.

00:00:20.934 --> 00:00:22.467
-Really?
-Yeah.

00:00:22.467 --> 00:00:25.067
Turns out he was just trying to
get Taylor Swift tickets.

00:00:25.067 --> 00:00:29.300
Yeah, that's all. It was fine.
The stars are just like us.

00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:30.901
Guys, it's Friday.
I'm in a great mood.

00:00:30.901 --> 00:00:32.734
Unlike Twitter,
we made it to the weekend.

00:00:32.734 --> 00:00:36.400
You know, and I --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:37.634
Did you see this?

00:00:37.634 --> 00:00:40.467
After more than
1,000 key employees resigned,

00:00:40.467 --> 00:00:42.501
Twitter closed
all of their offices.

00:00:42.501 --> 00:00:44.300
And, apparently,
due to the mass resignations,

00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:47.467
the platform could start
breaking soon.

00:00:47.467 --> 00:00:52.100
Even crypto was like, "Damn.
That came crashing down fast."

00:00:53.567 --> 00:00:55.434
Right now, things are so bad,
Twitter recommends

00:00:55.434 --> 00:00:56.734
writing your tweet on
a piece of paper

00:00:56.734 --> 00:00:59.901
and just mailing it to
all of your followers.

00:00:59.901 --> 00:01:02.167
Yeah, a ton of employees quit
after Elon asked them

00:01:02.167 --> 00:01:06.801
to commit to an extremely
hardcore work environment.

00:01:06.801 --> 00:01:09.067
Staff was like, "If I'm going to
go extremely hardcore

00:01:09.067 --> 00:01:10.400
for an app,
I don't want Twitter money.

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:13.200
I want OnlyFans money."

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:15.934
♪♪

00:01:15.934 --> 00:01:17.000
-Twitter.

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:19.000
-Last night, things got so bad,

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:22.767
the hashtag #RIPTwitter
started trending.

00:01:22.767 --> 00:01:26.434
I just want to say, I died on
Twitter before it was cool.

00:01:26.434 --> 00:01:28.033
[ Cheers and applause ]
No big deal.

00:01:28.033 --> 00:01:32.367
♪♪

00:01:32.367 --> 00:01:34.067
Some people say
the chaos at Twitter

00:01:34.067 --> 00:01:36.601
could lead to a comeback
for Tumblr.

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:39.868
That'd be fun to
get my political news

00:01:39.868 --> 00:01:42.200
at the same place I used to post
my Urkel fan fiction.

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:44.133
I think that'd be fun.

00:01:44.133 --> 00:01:46.033
Yeah, Twitter's not
looking so great right now,

00:01:46.033 --> 00:01:48.334
and I think some other companies
are trying to take advantage.

00:01:48.334 --> 00:01:49.467
Check out this.
I saw this today.

00:01:49.467 --> 00:01:51.834
-Twitter is
an absolute disaster,

00:01:51.834 --> 00:01:55.234
a horrible company that's
terribly run in every way.

00:01:55.234 --> 00:01:58.601
So when thinking of us,
remember, there's worse.

00:02:01.567 --> 00:02:03.934
-I go, "Oh, now I get it. Yeah.

00:02:03.934 --> 00:02:05.434
Now I get it."

00:02:07.968 --> 00:02:09.334
Some news from Washington.

00:02:09.334 --> 00:02:11.033
Tomorrow, President Biden's
granddaughter

00:02:11.033 --> 00:02:13.868
is getting married on the
South Lawn of The White House.

00:02:13.868 --> 00:02:15.000
That's nice. It's interesting.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:18.300
To RSVP, you had to check
"yes" or "Ivanka."

00:02:20.567 --> 00:02:22.801
Not gonna show up, no.

00:02:22.801 --> 00:02:24.067
Biden's already emotional.

00:02:24.067 --> 00:02:26.234
It's the first time an
80-year-old has ever said,

00:02:26.234 --> 00:02:28.067
"Get on my lawn.

00:02:30.434 --> 00:02:32.667
The South Lawn."

00:02:32.667 --> 00:02:33.934
It's different getting married

00:02:33.934 --> 00:02:35.133
when your grandfather's
president, though.

00:02:35.133 --> 00:02:36.868
You get cards that say,
"Enjoy the panini maker,

00:02:36.868 --> 00:02:39.767
love Kim Jong-un."

00:02:39.767 --> 00:02:42.300
Yeah, the Biden family has
a lot to celebrate this weekend,

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:44.801
'cause on Sunday,
the president turns 80.

00:02:44.801 --> 00:02:46.300
Wow.

00:02:46.300 --> 00:02:49.367
Just to give you the sense of
how old that is, consider this.

00:02:49.367 --> 00:02:51.467
He's 80.

00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:54.734
Democrats don't want to
take any chances,

00:02:54.734 --> 00:02:58.567
so there are going to be
no surprise parties.

00:02:58.567 --> 00:03:00.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:03.968 --> 00:03:07.701
Don't clap too loud.
He might be watching.

00:03:07.701 --> 00:03:09.033
Hey, this is big.

00:03:09.033 --> 00:03:10.267
Today, the Justice Department

00:03:10.267 --> 00:03:12.334
named a special counsel
to investigate whether

00:03:12.334 --> 00:03:15.601
former president Trump should be
charged for January 6th

00:03:15.601 --> 00:03:17.701
or taking classified documents.

00:03:17.701 --> 00:03:20.701
As we speak, Trump is squeezing
into a turkey costume

00:03:20.701 --> 00:03:22.934
to trick Biden
into pardoning him.

00:03:26.501 --> 00:03:28.300
[ As Trump ] Gobble, gobble.

00:03:29.601 --> 00:03:32.133
Gobble, gobble.

00:03:33.334 --> 00:03:35.467
[ Normal voice ] Switching
gears. Some big sports news.

00:03:35.467 --> 00:03:37.968
This weekend,
the World Cup begins in Qatar.

00:03:37.968 --> 00:03:40.701
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:40.701 --> 00:03:43.767
Yep. Soccer is huge
across the world.

00:03:43.767 --> 00:03:45.200
Meanwhile,
Americans are like, "Wait.

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:48.567
'Ted Lasso'
is based on a real sport?"

00:03:48.567 --> 00:03:49.701
Listen to this.

00:03:49.701 --> 00:03:51.100
On Sunday,
Elton John is performing

00:03:51.100 --> 00:03:53.067
his final concert in
North America,

00:03:53.067 --> 00:03:56.000
and the entire show will air
on Disney+.

00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:57.667
I just hope the
Disney product placement

00:03:57.667 --> 00:03:59.434
is a little more subtle than the
last time they worked with him.

00:03:59.434 --> 00:04:00.567
Check it out.

00:04:00.567 --> 00:04:02.567
-♪ D-D-D-D-Do what I say ♪

00:04:08.767 --> 00:04:12.534
-Speaking of Disney, I saw
that they just filed a patent

00:04:12.534 --> 00:04:13.667
for a new type of
roller coaster,

00:04:13.667 --> 00:04:14.801
and it looks pretty crazy.

00:04:14.801 --> 00:04:15.934
Watch this.

00:04:15.934 --> 00:04:18.501
-Walt Disney just filed a patent

00:04:18.501 --> 00:04:21.133
for a roller coaster
that jumps the track?

00:04:21.133 --> 00:04:23.100
Engineers say it has to move

00:04:23.100 --> 00:04:25.267
at precise speed
every single time,

00:04:25.267 --> 00:04:28.200
which can easily be impacted by
the weather, by humidity,

00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:31.334
number of riders,
and many, many other elements.

00:04:31.334 --> 00:04:34.868
[ Laughter ]
-Oh!

00:04:34.868 --> 00:04:37.734
-The ride is called You First.

00:04:37.734 --> 00:04:39.934
[ Rimshot ]

00:04:39.934 --> 00:04:41.367
Don't worry -- they're going to
put some pillows

00:04:41.367 --> 00:04:43.767
down the first few times they
try it, so it should be alright.

00:04:43.767 --> 00:04:45.267
It's the only ride
with a sign that says,

00:04:45.267 --> 00:04:47.300
"You must be this tall to die."

00:04:47.300 --> 00:04:48.367
But this is nice.

00:04:48.367 --> 00:04:49.767
Disney takes your picture
during the ride,

00:04:49.767 --> 00:04:53.901
and a crime-scene photographer
takes it after.

00:04:53.901 --> 00:04:56.100
"Jumps the tracks."

00:04:56.100 --> 00:04:57.667
Meanwhile,
Six Flags was like, "Big deal.

00:04:57.667 --> 00:04:59.767
We've been doing that
for years."

00:05:02.133 --> 00:05:04.100
Get this -- the makers of
Scrabble have announced

00:05:04.100 --> 00:05:06.167
that they now will accept
hundreds of new words.

00:05:06.167 --> 00:05:07.400
-Oh!

00:05:07.400 --> 00:05:09.167
-Check out this commercial they
just released.

00:05:09.167 --> 00:05:12.667
-America's most beloved
board game is better than ever,

00:05:12.667 --> 00:05:15.000
with hundreds of
new playable words, like...

00:05:17.701 --> 00:05:21.467
And to make it even more fun,
we now accept misspelled words,

00:05:21.467 --> 00:05:24.467
made-up words, and tater tots.

00:05:27.834 --> 00:05:29.467
-Interesting, right?
-Wow!

00:05:31.100 --> 00:05:33.567
Wow! Indeed.

00:05:33.567 --> 00:05:38.167
-Also, I read that Tyson Foods
recalled 94,000 pounds

00:05:38.167 --> 00:05:40.100
of ground beef
'cause it may contain

00:05:40.100 --> 00:05:42.801
a hard, mirror-like substance.

00:05:42.801 --> 00:05:46.234
They're really bending over
backwards to avoid saying,

00:05:46.234 --> 00:05:48.767
"Fine, it's glass, okay?"

00:05:48.767 --> 00:05:51.400
A "mirror-like substance"?

00:05:51.400 --> 00:05:53.200
Nothing worse than eating
a 1-pound burger

00:05:53.200 --> 00:05:55.133
and catching
a glimpse of yourself.

00:05:55.133 --> 00:05:57.267
"Ugh! That's what I look like?"

00:05:57.267 --> 00:05:59.701
Guys, it is the holiday season,

00:05:59.701 --> 00:06:02.367
and the Rockefeller Center
Christmas tree is here.

00:06:02.367 --> 00:06:03.934
If you guys haven't seen it yet,
here it is.

00:06:03.934 --> 00:06:06.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:06.834 --> 00:06:08.501
-Wow.

00:06:10.601 --> 00:06:12.901
-I don't want to say
anything too mean.

00:06:12.901 --> 00:06:14.767
It looks like it could use
some encouragement

00:06:14.767 --> 00:06:17.100
before its big lighting
later this month,

00:06:17.100 --> 00:06:18.567
so I wrote a tiny song.

00:06:18.567 --> 00:06:20.567
I hope you like it.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:30.634 --> 00:06:35.267
♪ You're 82 feet
and essentially flawless ♪

00:06:35.267 --> 00:06:39.968
♪ But we can't help but notice
you have male pattern baldness ♪

00:06:39.968 --> 00:06:44.267
♪ Just a week ago, we couldn't
wait for you to show up ♪

00:06:44.267 --> 00:06:46.534
♪ But now we're
all wondering when

00:06:46.534 --> 00:06:48.934
you'll g-g-g-g-glow up ♪

00:06:48.934 --> 00:06:53.467
♪ Time for a glow-up,
a Midtown makeover ♪

00:06:53.467 --> 00:06:57.601
♪ Let's get the "Queer Eye" guys
to do a t-t-t-t-takeover ♪

00:06:57.601 --> 00:07:02.167
♪ It's time for a glow-up,
you're looking pretty poor-ah ♪

00:07:02.167 --> 00:07:06.734
♪ So let's go get free samples
at S-S-S-S-Sephora ♪

00:07:06.734 --> 00:07:11.133
♪ It's time for a glow-up,
you might need to go faster ♪

00:07:11.133 --> 00:07:15.534
♪ We don't want to wait,
this isn't T-T-Ticketmaster ♪

00:07:15.534 --> 00:07:19.934
♪ It's time for a glow-up,
I know you're not a quitter ♪

00:07:19.934 --> 00:07:24.200
♪ At least you're doing better
than they are at T-T-T-Twitter ♪

00:07:24.200 --> 00:07:27.234
♪ It's time for glow-up ♪

00:07:28.701 --> 00:07:33.234
♪ It's time for glow-up ♪

00:07:33.234 --> 00:07:36.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:38.634 --> 00:07:40.133
Thank you.

00:07:40.133 --> 00:07:41.901
Thank you very much.

00:07:43.701 --> 00:07:45.501
And, finally, this is so cool.

00:07:45.501 --> 00:07:46.934
Last night, our pal Aaron Judge

00:07:46.934 --> 00:07:49.400
was named the American League's
Most Valuable Player.

00:07:49.400 --> 00:07:52.567
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:52.567 --> 00:07:55.400
And, of course, we wanted to do
something fun to celebrate.

00:07:55.400 --> 00:07:56.767
Take a look.

00:07:56.767 --> 00:07:59.567
We're at the MLB Flagship Store
here in New York City

00:07:59.567 --> 00:08:03.367
with my pal, the
American League MVP Aaron Judge.

00:08:03.367 --> 00:08:05.100
We're about to surprise
some baseball fans

00:08:05.100 --> 00:08:06.601
who think they're getting
their photo taken

00:08:06.601 --> 00:08:07.934
while pretending to pose

00:08:07.934 --> 00:08:10.400
in a batter's box
at Yankee Stadium.

00:08:10.400 --> 00:08:12.033
Because that's where I see you

00:08:12.033 --> 00:08:13.267
all the time --
in the batter's box.

00:08:13.267 --> 00:08:15.334
-[ Laughs ] Yeah.
You ready for this?

00:08:15.334 --> 00:08:17.000
-I'm ready for you to be, yeah,

00:08:17.000 --> 00:08:18.601
in the Yankee Stadium
all the time.

00:08:18.601 --> 00:08:21.200
That's the only place to see --
-Let's play ball.

00:08:21.200 --> 00:08:23.200
♪♪
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:08:27.033 --> 00:08:28.033
-Hello. How you doing?

00:08:28.033 --> 00:08:29.167
-This is our photographer,
Chris.

00:08:29.167 --> 00:08:30.300
He's going to set you up.

00:08:30.300 --> 00:08:31.534
-Okay, so, stand
in that batter's box.

00:08:31.534 --> 00:08:34.000
I'm going to go over here.
Okay, big smiles.

00:08:34.000 --> 00:08:36.033
And 1, 2, 3.

00:08:36.033 --> 00:08:37.601
[ Camera shutter clicks ]

00:08:37.601 --> 00:08:39.234
-Strike.

00:08:39.234 --> 00:08:41.234
I think that was a strike.
-I think it was a ball.

00:08:41.234 --> 00:08:42.868
-You do?
-Yeah.

00:08:42.868 --> 00:08:44.467
-Yeah, but can I make the call
on this?

00:08:44.467 --> 00:08:48.567
-I think I might do it.
[ Laughs ]

00:08:48.567 --> 00:08:50.701
-3, 2, 1.
-Here comes the pitch.

00:08:50.701 --> 00:08:53.000
-Str-i-i-i-ke!

00:08:53.000 --> 00:08:54.601
Strike!
[ Camera shutter clicks ]

00:08:54.601 --> 00:08:56.133
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:08:56.133 --> 00:08:57.334
Let's ask Aaron Judge.

00:08:57.334 --> 00:08:59.434
-Yeah, I thought I was
a little outside, too.

00:08:59.434 --> 00:09:00.968
-Yo!
-Yeah.

00:09:00.968 --> 00:09:02.601
We're on the same page here.
He's got a good eye.

00:09:02.601 --> 00:09:04.400
-No way.
-He's got a good eye.

00:09:04.400 --> 00:09:05.567
Yeah.
-[ Laughs ]

00:09:05.567 --> 00:09:08.000
-Str-i-i-i-ke 3!

00:09:08.000 --> 00:09:09.701
[ Camera shutter clicks ]

00:09:09.701 --> 00:09:11.100
-That's clearly a ball.

00:09:11.100 --> 00:09:13.033
Balls and strikes.

00:09:13.033 --> 00:09:15.467
-If Aaron Judge says
that it's a ball,

00:09:15.467 --> 00:09:17.634
then Jimmy Fallon says
it's a strike...

00:09:17.634 --> 00:09:20.234
-What do you guys think?
Ball or strike?

00:09:21.467 --> 00:09:23.934
[ Camera shutter clicks ]

00:09:23.934 --> 00:09:25.434
-Uh! That was a strike.

00:09:25.434 --> 00:09:26.801
-Ball 4.
-Strike!

00:09:26.801 --> 00:09:27.834
-Take your base.

00:09:27.834 --> 00:09:28.834
-Aah!
-That was a strike.

00:09:28.834 --> 00:09:29.834
[ Camera shutter clicks ]

00:09:29.834 --> 00:09:31.200
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:09:31.200 --> 00:09:32.667
-But who would you --
-[Bleep]

00:09:32.667 --> 00:09:33.934
-[ Laughs ]

00:09:33.934 --> 00:09:35.434
-One more, you're outta here.
You're outta here.

00:09:35.434 --> 00:09:36.934
-You're going to throw me
outta here?

00:09:36.934 --> 00:09:38.033
-That's it.

00:09:38.033 --> 00:09:39.467
-How can you throw me
outta here?

00:09:39.467 --> 00:09:40.667
-Oh, that's Jimmy Fallon.
-Jimmy...

00:09:40.667 --> 00:09:42.467
-This is Aaron Judge.

00:09:42.467 --> 00:09:43.701
-3, 2, 1.

00:09:43.701 --> 00:09:45.701
[ Camera shutter clicks ]
[ Laughter ]

00:09:45.701 --> 00:09:47.133
-What?!
-What?!

00:09:47.133 --> 00:09:48.567
-Hey.
-Jimmy?!

00:09:48.567 --> 00:09:50.033
-Yeah.
-What is going on?

00:09:50.033 --> 00:09:51.767
-You know Aaron Judge?

00:09:51.767 --> 00:09:53.234
-Yeah, like my body's
shaking right now.

00:09:55.167 --> 00:09:56.167
-Yeah.
-Sure.

00:09:56.167 --> 00:09:57.501
-Okay.

00:09:57.501 --> 00:09:58.501
-You want to stand on the box?
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:09:58.501 --> 00:10:00.334
-Yeah.
-Even better. Even better.

00:10:00.334 --> 00:10:01.400
-Well...

00:10:03.200 --> 00:10:05.601
[Indistinct]

00:10:05.601 --> 00:10:08.767
♪♪

00:10:08.767 --> 00:10:10.167
[ Cheering and applause ]
-Oh, my God!

00:10:11.100 --> 00:10:12.200
-We saw 60.
-[Indistinct]

00:10:12.200 --> 00:10:14.501
-Yes!

00:10:14.501 --> 00:10:16.801
-Let's get in the pic, too.
-Oh, my gosh. Yeah. What?

00:10:16.801 --> 00:10:19.234
[ Camera shutter clicks ]
♪♪

00:10:19.234 --> 00:10:21.133
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:10:21.133 --> 00:10:23.300
-My thanks
to Major League Baseball

00:10:23.300 --> 00:10:25.234
and the MLB Flagship Store

00:10:25.234 --> 00:10:27.534
and, of course, Aaron Judge!

00:10:27.534 --> 00:10:29.968
We love you, bud. Congrats.
We have a great show.

